      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 2216,
        "endIndex": 2627,
        "text": "### Candidate [6]: Samsung and SK Hynix reject KEPCO's ~$18.7B power prepayment proposal\n* **Publisher:** Reuters  \n* **Editorial Scope:** IN SCOPE  \n* **What is confirmed:** A South Korean parliamentary document reveals that Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix rejected a proposal by state utility KEPCO to prepay 25 trillion won (~$18.7B) to fund power grid infrastructure for planned semiconductor mega-clusters"
